  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 24d0b860ee; owner-requested re-check of the 51 open P2 violated/todo_hard/todo_soft items; fixtures and outputs under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p2_review_11012026/B1/). VERDICT: CURRENT; the item's own fixtures are confounded. All --no-default-overlays: unannotated `let child = ...spawn().unwrap()` -> 0 rows, exit 2, caveat 'receiver's type could not be determined - stdout, wait_with_output'; adding `use std::process::Child` (v2a), a brace list (v2b), plain spawn() (v2d) -> still 0; annotated `let child: std::process::Child` with NO Child import -> 1 row, precise; `?` behaves like .unwrap(). So the annotation is the discriminator and the import is irrelevant. CAUSE of the 'NOT CHECKED': library_signatures/ has go/java/objc/python/swift and NO rust file, so rule 5 of _extract_var_types_rust (rust.py:508-515) has no return type for Command::spawn; the builder chain is not the cause (v2d has none). CONFOUND: rust.py var_types is FILE-scoped (rust.py:412, 493-497), so in the item's 5-function fixture the one annotated `child` typed every `child` and all five reported, including unannotated_q - filed today as a separate false-positive-direction defect. ACCEPTANCE should add: a passing test must not share a file with an annotated same-named binding. rust.py changes since (892d4912cb, 9591306872) do not touch let typing. ROOT-CAUSE GROUP: receiver type not carried to the emission site (with WI-mofil, WI-fihun, WI-vogip). Status unchanged."  # 3791
